          "heading": "Outcomes and a practical engineering question",
          "content": "## Outcomes and a practical engineering question\n\nBy the end of this unit, a student should be able to translate the geologic observations in **investigation methods and geophysical interpretation** into a documented alternative ground model, quantify at least one relevant sensitivity, and explain what additional evidence would change the decision. The goal is not memorization of terms but a defendable sequence: observation \u2192 interpretation \u2192 process model \u2192 engineering implication \u2192 uncertainty.\n\nA usable field record contains the datum, location, measurement method, orientation or depth, date, observer, evidence strength and confidence. A drawing without those attributes is difficult to audit when field conditions change."
